     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nSome possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** This would be 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **A different dose entirely.** For example, 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you meant, tell me and I'll add a note documenting that it was confirmed. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
